z9x-0008: no takeover through an AirPlay (video) connection; mirror data port only for the sender

Ours (Z9xAirPlay), against FDH2/UxPlay master 3dbf7ce after z9x-0001..0007 (paths relative
to UxPlay/lib). Applied by jni/build_native.sh inside a copy of UxPlay/lib with
patch -p1 --fuzz=0.
- raop.c: a new connection without CSeq but with X-Apple-Session-ID (AirPlay video) used to
  stop the running sender's mirror, audio and NTP services unconditionally. Without
  nohold it now gets 409 when a RAOP connection from another address exists.
- raop_rtp_mirror.c: the mirror data socket accepted the first TCP connection from anyone;
  a connection from an address other than the session's RTSP peer is closed and the port
  keeps listening.
